    <briefdescription>
<para>Google Benchmark performance tests for streaming window runtime limit hardening. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Covers the Q3 2026 roadmap item: &quot;hardening of streaming and distributed runtime limits
under sustained load&quot; (src/analytics/ROADMAP.md).</para>
<para>Benchmarks:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>BM_TumblingWindow_IngestThroughput – baseline throughput, 1 M records</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>BM_TumblingWindow_SustainedLoad_Bounded – same with max_open_windows=10 (eviction overhead)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>BM_TumblingWindow_FlushLatency – flush() latency with N open windows</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>BM_SlidingWindow_IngestThroughput – baseline throughput</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>BM_SlidingWindow_RecordLimitDrop – throughput with max_records_per_window enforced</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>BM_SessionWindow_IngestThroughput – baseline throughput, multi-key</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>BM_SessionWindow_BoundedSessions – throughput with max_open_sessions=50 (eviction)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Measurement hygiene:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Canonical seed: 42</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>No file I/O; all data in-memory</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>UseRealTime() for all benchmarks (wall-clock; scheduler jitter amortised over 1 M ops) </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
